{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh's direction, 2026-10-11 16:50 Eastern: update the demo plan with the rules requirements for the concurrent-edit story, and record the positioning.\n\nPositioning. The lead claim of the video and the public material is: dap is a programmable, general-purpose coordination fabric. The verifier line (\"nothing you saw depends on trusting our database\") stays as a supporting proof, not the way in. Order of the video: open on the repository story (issue, comment, assign, change, refusal under rules, approval, publication); then the same fabric running the Counter; then the same fabric running the jam; then back to the repository (\"that is why the Git story can be whatever your team's rules say\"). Put the concurrency beat early, and state the hosting surface in one line: the Worker, the hosting's own Git service as the repository host, the published pages, and the same record running on GitHub.\n\nThe concurrent-edit story is a three-step ladder, each step a recorded act with a named reason, and no textual merge anywhere:\n\n1. Prevented by rule. A concern of a plan declares the paths it covers (a field on add-concern). A report whose tree, against the concern's base, touches a path outside its concern is refused with a named reason (for example path-outside-concern). Reuse the extents classifier in packages/platform/src/extents.ts for the path judgment. Because lanes are data, this is a definition change in packages/lanes plus the guard's code, and the demo says so. The builder estimates it against the freeze; if it does not fit, the beat becomes one narrated line over the existing refusal shot.\n\n2. Composed by selection. One issue, a sealed plan with two concerns, two agents each under a hold (each in its own fork once the forks plan lands; until then, each under its grant and hold as the record already enforces). Each returns a report. The integrator proposes a manifest selecting both reports. The destination checks that both report commits are ancestors and the base is the head, and publishes one integration commit. Said: \"nothing merged this; the room checked that it was composed from exactly these two accepted pieces\".\n\n3. Refused when stale. Two changes on the same base; the first publishes; the second is refused out-of-date (reservation check 1) and is re-proposed on the new head by its integrator. Add this as a shot to the demo runner (docs/demo.md), with its expected lines from an observed run. Said: \"the loser is not patched by a model; it is re-proposed under the same rules\".\n\nThe plan names, for each step: what exists on main today, what the builder must build, the acceptance witness, and the fallback if the freeze passes first. Keep landings and deployments ahead of this work; the rehearsal shot for step 3 is the cheapest and goes first. See plans/024-2026-10-06-demo-plan-to-the-14th.md, plans/019-2026-10-05-demo-story-direction.md, plans/016-2026-10-05-repository-extents-demo.md, docs/lanes.md, packages/platform/src/reservation.ts.","body":{"conditions":"Plan 024 updated on main, or a dated successor plan, carrying the positioning, the three-step concurrency ladder and its rules requirements; the demo shot list (notes/2026-10-07-demo-script-draft.md or its successor) revised to match; builder requests filed for the concern path guard and the stale-base rehearsal shot, each with the builder's estimate against the 2026-10-12 freeze; the checker queue order unchanged ahead of them. The planner reports the commits in the sprint-cadence thread and in the next sprint report.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}